    "question": "How sustainable are the margins, and how much of the Q1 expansion is one-off?",
    "answer": "Management said the export margin was boosted by optical fiber opportunities that may not recur every quarter; domestic electrical margin of about 10.5% should be sustainable, and communication margins should fall to low double digits by year-end."
   },
   {
    "question": "What is the expected preform-backed margin uplift once backward integration is complete?",
    "answer": "Management declined to quantify a 100 bps uplift, saying fiber prices are demand-driven and may cool once data center demand reaches a steady state; input costs such as helium are fluctuating."
   },
   {
    "question": "What is the revenue potential of the fiber capacity at current prices?",
    "answer": "At 8 million fiber km and about USD 11/km, fiber-only revenue would be about USD 88 million (roughly INR 250-260 crore per 4 million km quarter basis as discussed); cabling adds about 25-30% value-add depending on design."
   },
   {
    "question": "Is the INR 5 billion FMEG target by FY28 still realistic?",
    "answer": "Management said Q1 was hit by LPG shortages for fan makers and PVC issues for conduit pipes; the target of INR 5 billion by FY28 is still in place."
   },
   {
    "question": "Is the export surge repeatable and what is the export pipeline?",
    "answer": "Management said Q1 exports were opportunistic, but a revamped export-only team is building relationships across multiple geographies, with no guaranteed mix going forward."
   },
   {
    "question": "What share of communication cable revenue is long-term versus spot?",
    "answer": "Long-term contracts still make up more than half of communication cable revenue; repricing of these contracts happened in June 2026."
